                        <div class="project-description">

                            <p>
                                Developed a C++ implementation of Conway's Game
                                of Life, a cellular automata simulation in which
                                cells change between active and inactive states
                                based on the condition of neighboring cells.
                            </p>

                            <p>
                                Applied object-oriented programming principles
                                to organize the simulation into reusable and
                                maintainable classes. Created logic for grid
                                initialization, neighboring-cell calculations,
                                state transitions, simulation updates, and
                                console-based output.
                            </p>

                            <p>
                                The project demonstrates algorithm design,
                                conditional logic, loops, multidimensional data
                                structures, debugging, program organization, and
                                the implementation of mathematical rules within
                                a software simulation.
                            </p>

                        </div>

                    </div>

